     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You aren't the prescriber.** Confirming it yourself doesn't count as clinician verification. The prescriber needs to confirm the dose.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg per day is twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't make that dose safe.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Ask the prescribing clinician to review the order. If they intended a different dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, they can tell me and I'll enter it.\n- If a prescriber really does want a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves through the normal channels. Pharmacy review will then apply.\n\nI'm glad to help with the entry once a clinician has confirmed a dose in the standard range."
      }
     ],
